From: Majid Arasskhani <M.Arasskhani@gosilkroad.net>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 15:41:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/22] perf: move psutil sampling, audio temp-file I/O and
 base64 encoding off the event loop

Bug (B-10): _collect_system_metrics called psutil.cpu_percent(interval=0.15)
and Process.cpu_percent(interval=0.1) inline - a 250 ms sleep on the event
loop per admin refresh and per hourly metrics snapshot, stalling every
request on that worker. The LiteLLM transcription path wrote up to 25 MB of
audio to a temp file and unlinked it synchronously; the OpenRouter path
base64-encoded the same bytes inline.

Change: db_monitor_service.collect_system_metrics() runs the sampler in a
thread and both callers await it; transcription_service writes/removes the
temp file via asyncio.to_thread helpers; openrouter_transcription_service
encodes in a thread. Attachment text extraction was moved earlier (2.5).

Tests: tests/test_blocking_work_off_loop.py - a 300 ms sampler leaves loop
tick gaps under 100 ms; the OpenRouter payload still carries the exact
base64 of the audio; temp file helpers run in threads and are idempotent;
readiness pings through the shared Redis client without closing it.

